From d65daf640ea551d4aed0e1060f274e1c4116889f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:15:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:sigma_dut: Fix -Y consuming the next argv
 token as its argument

main() builds its getopt() option string as:

  "aAb:Bc:C:dDE:e:fF:gGhH:j:J:i:Ik:K:l:L:m:M:nN:o:O:p:P:qQr:R:s:S:tT:uU:v:VWw:xX:yY:z:Z:2345:6:7"

The "Y:" entry declares that -Y takes a mandatory argument. However
case 'Y' (main(), sigma_dut.c) never reads optarg -- it only does
"log_to_file = 1;" and breaks, i.e. -Y was always intended to be a
bare on/off flag, matching every other logging toggle (-d, -D) in
the same switch.

files/sigma_dut.init builds the daemon's ARGS as:

  [ "${debug}" == on ] && append ARGS "-Y -d "

so when "option debug 'on'" is set in /etc/config/sigma-dut, argv
ends up containing "-Y" immediately followed by the separate token
"-d". Because the option string declares Y as requiring an argument,
getopt() consumes that next token, the literal string "-d", as -Y's
optarg instead of parsing it as its own option. case 'Y' ignores
that consumed optarg (so -Y's own effect, enabling log_to_file, is
unaffected), but case 'd' never runs, so dut->debug_level stays at
its default DUT_MSG_INFO instead of dropping to DUT_MSG_DEBUG.

The effect: sigma_dut_print() calls at DUT_MSG_INFO (cmd/resp/"Run
command" lines) keep appearing in /tmp/sigma.txt, but every
DUT_MSG_DEBUG line -- most importantly run_system()'s "Running '%s'"
trace of the actual shell/iw/fwtest commands issued for each CAPI
call -- is filtered out by the "if (level < dut->debug_level) return;"
check in sigma_dut_print(), even though "option debug 'on'" is set.
This only reproduces when -Y and -d arrive as separate argv tokens
(e.g. via the init script); invoking sigma_dut manually with a single
combined token such as "-dddt" is unaffected, since no -Y precedes it
to consume "-d".

Fix by removing the stray ":" after Y in the getopt() option string,
matching the flag's actual (argument-less) implementation in case 'Y'.

Signed-off-by: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 sigma_dut.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sigma_dut.c b/sigma_dut.c
index 1c12016..47a4e2c 100644
--- a/sigma_dut.c
+++ b/sigma_dut.c
@@ -1152,7 +1152,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 
 	for (;;) {
 		c = getopt(argc, argv,
-			   "aAb:Bc:C:dDE:e:fF:gGhH:j:J:i:Ik:K:l:L:m:M:nN:o:O:p:P:qQr:R:s:S:tT:uU:v:VWw:xX:yY:z:Z:2345:6:7");
+			   "aAb:Bc:C:dDE:e:fF:gGhH:j:J:i:Ik:K:l:L:m:M:nN:o:O:p:P:qQr:R:s:S:tT:uU:v:VWw:xX:yYz:Z:2345:6:7");
 		if (c < 0)
 			break;
 		switch (c) {
-- 
